The number of Collatz steps for n to reach 1: halve an even number, and take three times it plus one for an odd one. Zero never reaches 1, so it loops until the fuel runs out, which is the outcome out_of_fuel.
The probe is a loop with a numeric exit condition, and an input that never meets it.
---
---
(fn n
  (letrec steps
    (fn (k acc)
      (if (= k 1)
        acc
        (if (= (mod k 2) 0) (steps (div k 2) (+ acc 1)) (steps (+ (* 3 k) 1) (+ acc 1)))))
    (steps n 0)))
---
1 => 0 fuel 100000
2 => 1 fuel 100000
6 => 8 fuel 100000
7 => 16 fuel 100000
27 => 111 fuel 100000
0 => out_of_fuel fuel 10000
